mate. Markets and most raters keep Boebert favored.", "watch": "Any independent polling or outside spending confirming Laubacher's financial edge is translating into a tied race would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Lauren Boebert (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Lauren Boebert seeks reelection in a district that leans Republican by about nine points, but this has become an unusually competitive contest. Challenger Eileen Laubacher has raised over $10 million, dwarfing Boebert's roughly $1 million and leaving her with a large cash advantage heading into the final weeks. A September live-caller poll of likely voters showed Boebert ahead by only five points, and several raters now call the race a Tossup, though others still rate it Likely or Solid Republican.\n\nPrediction markets give Boebert roughly a 70 percent chance, and the district's partisan lean remains a real obstacle for a Democrat. The forecast keeps Boebert favored by a modest margin, with elevated uncertainty given thin polling and the scale of Democratic spending still untested at the ballot box.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3037, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.297, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2256, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-10-